## Why This Is Asked

Explores runtime extensibility and safe composition of resilience patterns (Strategy + Decorator) at scale, mirroring needs in large tech orgs where policies evolve without touching core call logic.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern: policy abstraction
- Chain of Responsibility / Decorator: pipeline composition
- Registry pattern: runtime extensibility
- Trade-offs: backoffs, timeout precision, isolation

## Code Example

```typescript
type Request = { url: string; payload?: any }
type Response = any
type Next = () => Promise<Response>

interface Policy {
  handle(req: Request, next: Next): Promise<Response>
}
type PolicyFactory = (ctx?: any) => Policy

class PolicyRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, PolicyFactory>()
  register(name: string, factory: PolicyFactory) { this.map.set(name, factory) }
  create(name: string, ctx?: any): Policy | null { const f = this.map.get(name); return f ? f(ctx) : null }
}
```

